const checkIds = new Set(CHECK_CATALOG.map(c => c.check_id));
if (checkIds.size !== CHECK_CATALOG.length) throw new Error('Duplicate check ID');
for (const vector of VECTOR_LIBRARY) for (const id of vector.check_ids ?? []) if (!checkIds.has(id)) throw new Error(`Unknown vector mapping ${id}`);

const sections = [];
sections.push(section('overview', 'What AstraNull currently is', `
<p>AstraNull is an <strong>outside-in DDoS readiness and protection validation platform</strong> for customer-declared domains, URLs, IPs and service endpoints. It helps an engineering or security team answer: which public paths respond, which bounded markers are blocked, where protection evidence is missing, and what needs remediation. Cloud/CDN credentials are optional. Customer-installed agents and environments are outside the current product model (ADR-0008).</p>
<p>This document describes the <strong>local working tree captured ${esc(generatedAt)}</strong>, package ${esc(JSON.parse(read('package.json')).version)}, based on Git commit <code>${esc(commit)}</code>. ${workingTreeChanges.length ? 'It includes uncommitted changes listed in the snapshot metadata.' : 'The working tree was clean at generation.'} It is a passive documentation snapshot; generating or opening it sends no probes and does not certify the deployed service.</p>
<div class="notice"><strong>Three different things:</strong> the library contains ${VECTOR_LIBRARY.length} named attack/availability vectors; the executable/declaration catalog contains ${CHECK_CATALOG.length} check definitions; a particular target can run only its compatible, authorized, configured subset. These numbers are not ${VECTOR_LIBRARY.length} proven attacks or ${CHECK_CATALOG.length} complete live tests.</div>
${table(['Catalog classification','Count','What it establishes'], [
 ['All check definitions', CHECK_CATALOG.length, 'Complete inventory below; generated directly from CHECK_CATALOG'],
 ['Customer safe definitions',count(c=>c.safety_class).safe,'Selectable subject to target, ownership, setup, feature and safety gates'],
 ['SOC-gated definitions',count(c=>c.safety_class).soc_gated,'Governed request/workflow; no customer self-service traffic executor'],
 ['E1 declaration only',count(c=>c.evidence_tier).E1,'No network I/O; remains inconclusive'],
 ['E2 observations',count(c=>c.evidence_tier).E2,'Transport/provider facts; no readiness credit'],
 ['E3 semantic safe',count(c=>c.evidence_tier).E3,'Bounded fact or heuristic; assurance is limited per executor'],
 ['E4 governed',count(c=>c.evidence_tier).E4,'Requires SOC workflow and retained evidence'],
])}
<p>The retained release includes public entry, signup, customer portal, staff administration and SOC console. Older agent/bootstrap/environment docs and routes remain in parts of the repository; their presence is legacy compatibility, not a restored agent product. Customer workflows select domains directly; legacy group policy/storage/scoring remains internally. ${link('docs/implementation/target-only-domain-workflows.md')}</p>`));

